---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const title = "Personal Loan APR Comparison";
const description =
  "Compare personal loan APR offers by aligning term, fees, and cash received. Educational use only.";

const lastUpdated = "2026-02-17";
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonicalPath="/guides/personal-loan-apr-comparison" lastUpdated={lastUpdated} robots="noindex, follow">
  <section class="card hero">
    <span class="pill">Guide</span>
    <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/">Home</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/guides">Guides</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span aria-current="page">Personal loan APR</span>
    </nav>
    <h1>Personal loan APR comparison</h1>
    <p>
      Personal loan offers can look similar until you compare fees, term, and cash received. Use this guide to compare
      APR on a consistent basis.
    </p>
    <div class="btn-row">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/calculators/apr-calculator">APR calculator</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/guides/apr-vs-interest-rate">Interest rate vs APR</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/topics/apr">APR topic</a>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">APR comparison inputs to verify</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Loan amount and term (keep them constant across offers).</li>
      <li>Nominal rate vs APR and which fees are included.</li>
      <li>Upfront fees paid in cash vs financed.</li>
      <li>Expected time horizon before refinance or payoff.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">What to align</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Same loan amount and term.</li>
      <li>Same fee treatment (paid upfront vs financed).</li>
      <li>Same time horizon if you might prepay.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Why APR can differ</h2>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0">
      Origination fees reduce the net amount you receive, which increases the effective cost. APR captures that effect
      more consistently than rate alone.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Offer comparison checklist</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Net cash received after fees.</li>
      <li>Total dollars paid over your payoff horizon.</li>
      <li>Prepayment penalty or minimum interest rules.</li>
      <li>Autopay discounts or rate step-ups after missed payments.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Decision checks</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Compare APR and total cost for the same term.</li>
      <li>Confirm whether fees are financed or paid upfront.</li>
      <li>Verify how payments change if you prepay early.</li>
      <li>Re-run the comparison if you change the loan term.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Decision inputs</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Net cash you need after fees and deductions.</li>
      <li>Monthly payment ceiling that fits your budget.</li>
      <li>Rate discounts for autopay or relationship pricing.</li>
      <li>Prepayment flexibility and any minimum interest rules.</li>
      <li>Planned payoff horizon if you expect early payoff.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Funding timeline</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Confirm when funds are disbursed and when interest starts.</li>
      <li>Check if there is a short payoff window to avoid extra interest.</li>
      <li>Match the funding speed to your actual cash need.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Common mistakes</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Comparing offers with different terms.</li>
      <li>Ignoring fees or lender credits.</li>
      <li>Using rate instead of APR as the main comparison.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="grid" style="margin-top:18px">
    <div class="card section prose col-6">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0">Related tools</h2>
      <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
        <li><a href="/calculators/apr-calculator">APR calculator</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="card section prose col-6">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0">Related guides</h2>
      <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
        <li><a href="/guides/apr-with-origination-fee">APR with origination fee</a></li>
        <li><a href="/guides/apr-with-origination-fee">APR when fees are financed</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">FAQ</h2>
    <h3 style="margin:12px 0 0">Is the lowest APR always the best?</h3>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:8px 0 0">
      Often, but not always. If you plan to prepay early, compare total dollars over your horizon.
    </p>
    <h3 style="margin:12px 0 0">Do personal loans have prepayment penalties?</h3>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:8px 0 0">
      Many do not, but confirm in the loan documents before assuming early payoff is free.
    </p>
  </section>

    <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">References</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>
        CFPB:{" "}
        <a href="https://www.consumerfinance.gov/ask-cfpb/what-is-apr-and-why-is-it-higher-than-my-interest-rate-en-156/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">
          What is APR and why is it higher than my interest rate?
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        CFPB:{" "}
        <a href="https://www.consumerfinance.gov/ask-cfpb/what-is-a-loan-estimate-en-195/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">
          What is a Loan Estimate?
        </a>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

<section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Next steps</h2>
    <div class="btn-row" style="margin-top:10px">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/calculators/apr-calculator">Compare APR offers</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/guides/apr-with-origination-fee">APR with origination fee</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/topics/apr">APR topic</a>
    </div>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:12px 0 0">Educational use only. Not financial advice.</p>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:12px 0 0; font-size:13px">Last updated: 2026-02-17</p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>





